231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (I wish I could say that I hope this letter finds you well, but at this precise moment, I cannot. Not a few hours ago, our people were burned alive in Gaza. And as I sit here, writing this, I cannot help but feel helpless. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
232 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (I cannot currently go to Gaza and save lives, and I do not know if I will be able to do that in the future. What I can do, is speak about it, raise funds, scream out into the world about the unfairness of it all. AUSSS is that space for me, as it is for all of you. This unique place joined us all in a cocooned community, where we keep each other safe, and that encourages us to do what we are most passionate about. AUSSS let me be a photographer, a writer, a speaker, an advocate, an event planner, a project manager, it even gave me an underpaid \(ops not paid\) 9-5 job; except, well, the hours are not that strict. In short, I will never be just a doctor, and for that I will never stop being grateful. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (My experience in IFMSA cannot be summed up in one role or one committee. From logistics team \(I know, what is that?\) to the Trainers Pool Advisory Board, I left nothing untouched, my first campaign was in SCORA, my first debate in SCOME, my first workshop in exchange, my first physical campaign in SCOPH, I learned most from SCORP, I handled the online pages, I took part in OCs locally and nationally, I helped in outgoing campaigns and I have welcomed our incomings. I found my place in the CBSD and internal development, and I stayed. I tried everything, all to prepare for this very moment. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (This past year has been unusual for me in IFMSA, I had to step away locally and the beauty of the work that I loved left me. This feeling you get in AUSSS? You do not get it anywhere else. At some point, the friends I made here became the friends I want to keep for life, and the work we do? The posts, the physical campaigns, the sessions, the toolkits, the magazines, the check-ins, the community, they are all things I will fondly look back to. However, we have much to do. This last year with IFMSA-Egypt on hiatus, we were grounded. It set us back and it should never have been this way. )
/E (This past year has been unusual for me in IFMSA, I had to step away locally and the beauty of the work that I loved left me. This feeling you get in AUSSS? You do not get it anywhere else. At some point, the friends I made here became the friends I want to keep for life, and the work we do? The posts, the physical campaigns, the sessions, the toolkits, the magazines, the check-ins, the community, they are all things I will fondly look back to. However, we have much to do. This last year with IFMSA-Egypt on hiatus, we were grounded. It set us back and it should never have been this way. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (We lost sight of what truly mattered, and our passion? we lost it. I got to see so many new people get engaged with new ideas, new possibilities and the world seemed so much brighter, but the members who were already here? Who gave this LC so much of their time and wit have burnt out.)
/E (We lost sight of what truly mattered, and our passion? we lost it. I got to see so many new people get engaged with new ideas, new possibilities and the world seemed so much brighter, but the members who were already here? Who gave this LC so much of their time and wit have burnt out.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (I want to be president to set balance. Reengage the OGs, because I was once engaged because of them. I am still here because of the support of those around me. Those who stood by me and taught me, and as we start this new year, we want new people, new ideas, but we also need a reason, a place for them to want to stay. The work we do is amazing, but it takes a toll. Because as much as we say we make change, it is a tediously slow process, and when someone forgets, we need a strong community to remind them why we are all here. I want us to have a strong base, to have every current member of AUSSS ready and willing to give their best so we can inspire newly recruited members to do the same.)
/E (I want to be president to set balance. Reengage the OGs, because I was once engaged because of them. I am still here because of the support of those around me. Those who stood by me and taught me, and as we start this new year, we want new people, new ideas, but we also need a reason, a place for them to want to stay. The work we do is amazing, but it takes a toll. Because as much as we say we make change, it is a tediously slow process, and when someone forgets, we need a strong community to remind them why we are all here. I want us to have a strong base, to have every current member of AUSSS ready and willing to give their best so we can inspire newly recruited members to do the same.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
238 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (I will not lie to you and tell you it is all sunshine and rainbows. The world is a cruel place. Nonetheless, I can promise to fight with you, hold your hand and wipe your frustrated tears, because I get it. We are here because we want something more, and I will do my very best to ensure that AUSSS is the space where you become your something more, always. Hand in hand, with our joint experiences, we will make this world a better place.)
/E (I will not lie to you and tell you it is all sunshine and rainbows. The world is a cruel place. Nonetheless, I can promise to fight with you, hold your hand and wipe your frustrated tears, because I get it. We are here because we want something more, and I will do my very best to ensure that AUSSS is the space where you become your something more, always. Hand in hand, with our joint experiences, we will make this world a better place.)
